sition's `source-index`, fetch and admission): build NO resolver of your own, the holder's export passes the composition's index as `rows/lift-task`'s `:source-index`, the carried `:yin.k/trees` association stays as the receiver's completeness check; BLAKE3; no backward compatibility or version dispatch (the old codec versions 0/1/2 are not rewritten or kept alive by shims: delete only what 7b replaces: the version-1 export-recovery object and the holder's use of `export-task`/`resume-task`); lease/epoch/holder never enter a body; `:resume-mode` v2 is out.\n5\tImplement 7b as the plan's slice and 3.2 say: `holder/export.cljc` (`prepare`/`encode` over `rows/lift-task` with `:header` and a `:serve-keyed` adaptor; `freeze` produces recovery v2: the second snapshot body is gone, rows carry the whole store and every parked record, the object keeps only holder-local engine state (gate, issues, issued, origins) beside the pack; `rehydrate-fenced` over `lower-task {:fenced true}`; finish `:fenced`: `:yin.k/recovery-cell-ids`, the exact id counter, parked records into the record, the header check against `:yin.k/state`), `holder/driver.cljc` (`lower`, `step-validating`, `rebuilt-cell`, `reopen-holder`, `reopen-exit`; `source-mint`/`exit-mint` unchanged in shape; `:export-version` removed), `compose.cljc` (`holder-config-keys`/`driver-config` drop `:export-version`), tests `holder/export_test`, `holder/driver_test` (117 deftests), `holder/writer_test`, `holder/reader_test`, `holder/evidence_test` (machines from `rows_support`; rec1 rows replaced; the v2 fork-lift deftest deleted), `handoff_v2_holder_test` (one deftest deleted). Preserve D4's fact (the lift serves streams before an exhaustion or protection refusal) in the export record's accounting and test it. Acceptance (plan 7b): recovery v2 freezes and rehydrates fenced with zero program IO, the published pack reproduced byte for byte, aliases and distinct cursor cells preserved, install children rehydrated without initialization or IO, a restarted abort refused; `driver_test` whole, `writer_test`, `reader_test`, `evidence_test` green; the law \"zero attachments before the custody stage refuses\" pinned by attach counts; the Q3 install checks with refusals tested. If the plan and the code disagree, the code wins: report it as a design defect, do not silently change semantics. Portability: `.cljc` JVM, Node, Dart (no `for` over possibly long seqs, no private var access, `(assoc {} ...)`, no unary minus on floats, `#?(:cljd nil :clj ...)` order, catches `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)`); slow cases `^:slow` + `dao.test-slow/guard`.\n6\tVerification, ALL foreground, JVM only: `clj -M:kondo --lint <changed files>`; `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n <each touched ns>` then `-i :slow`; every `yin.vm.ucf.holder.*` and authority namespace; `rows_test`, the safepoint harness, `layout_test` unchanged (no existing root id moves). compose/fencing/stage-e suites stay red until 7c/7d: list them, do not touch them. No Node/Dart. Mutants (cp backup; diff and `git diff --quiet` to verify): freeze keeps a snapshot body; rehydrate-fenced runs program code; an id counter off by one on rehydrate; a parked record dropped on freeze; the abort restart accepted; the Q3 checks removed one at a time; export serves without the source index; lower attaches before custody. Report which mutants the tests catch. Do not commit. Report `collab/1792450000000-engineer-7b-holder-export.report.md`: files with line counts, test counts, mutation table, deviations, design defects (separate list), what 7c needs.\n7\t\n8\t\n9\tRESUME NOTE: a previous run of this brief died on a usage limit after about 32 minutes and left a LARGE UNCOMMITTED edit in this worktree (driver.cljc, export.cljc, compose.cljc, rows.cljc, the holder/handoff/rows_* tests; no report). First run `git diff --stat` and `git diff` and review it critically: keep what is correct and complete, redo what is not. Do not start over blindly and do not r