{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014eip4YzG8s7ArTH72Pz5Mi","type":"tool_result","content":"1730\t(defn lift-task\n1731\t  \"The lift of §7.1: quiescent semantic-register machine m as a version-3\n1732\t   carrier, or a refusal thrown as ex-data {:yin.k/status :yin.k/kind}.\n1733\t   serve! is the exporter's remote-table entry (yin.vm.ucf.remote).\n1734\t   opts: :free-env, the task's initial free environment (default: the\n1735\t   kernel's retained :free-env field; the explicit value overrides it);\n1736\t   :source-index, {A #{tree-address}} the composition knows (§6.1), which\n1737\t   must cover every carried segment; :budget, the numbering budget;\n1738\t   :header, the exclusive custody header (occurrence, arbitration,\n1739\t   next-op-seq, origin when the task has a predecessor, and\n1740\t   :yin.k/enrolled, the enrolled stream identities, a lift input that\n1741\t   never travels); :serve-keyed, (f [task-path resource-id] handle), which\n1742\t   replaces serve! and is asked once per resource of each task, the task\n1743\t   path being the install names from the root ([] for the root itself),\n1744\t   so a caller can retain each answer under its key (holder.export's\n1745\t   record). No header is the fork: custody nil. A header writes the\n1746\t   root's slot by kind (header-custody), refuses :op-seq-exhausted at\n1747\t   2^52-1 on a blocked or parked root, and protects every retained write\n1748\t   of the tree (protect!). Before emitting, the lift runs custody-baseline\n1749\t   over the task, so it never emits a carrier the inspector refuses.\"\n1750\t  ([m serve!] (lift-task m serve! {}))\n1751\t  ([m serve! opts]\n1752\t   (let [opts (or opts {})\n1753\t         header (:header opts)\n1754\t         task (lift-task* m serve! opts :root)\n1755\t         kind (nth (:slots task) 2)\n1756\t         task (if (nil? header)\n1757\t                task\n1758\t                (let [n (:yin.k/next-op-seq header)]\n1759\t                  (when (and (not= :halted kind) (cbor/numeric? n) (cbor/num= n max-exact))\n1760\t                    (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :op-seq-exhausted {:yin.k/next-op-seq n}))\n1761\t                  (protect! task (or (:yin.k/enrolled header) #{}))\n1762\t                  (assoc-in task [:slots 16] (header-custody header kind))))]\n1763\t     (custody-baseline task)\n1764\t     (emit task (merge default-budget (:budget opts))))))\n1765\t\n1766\t\n1767\t(def ^:private fixed-resource-keys\n1768\t  #{vm/call-in-stream-key vm/call-out-stream-key vm/call-out-cursor-key\n1769\t    module/link-request-resource module/link-response-resource})\n1770\t\n1771\t\n1772\t(defn- fresh-key!\n1773\t  [used]\n1774\t  (loop [n (inc (count @used))]\n1775\t    (let [k (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"k-\" n))]\n1776\t      (if (contains? @used k) (recur (inc n)) (do (swap! used conj k) k)))))\n1777\t\n1778\t\n1779\t(defn- rows-of\n1780\t  \"Every row of kind under n; install children too unless own-only.\"\n1781\t  [n kind own-only?]\n1782\t  (let [out (atom [])]\n1783\t    (letfn [(visit\n1784\t              [n]\n1785\t              (when (= kind (:kind n)) (swap! out conj n))\n1786\t              (doseq [[d x] (map vector (descriptors (:kind n) (:slots n)) (:slots n))]\n1787\t                (cond\n1788\t                  (and (ref? d) (= :task (:kind x))) (when-not own-only? (visit x))\n1789\t                  (ref? d) (visit x)\n1790\t                  (refs? d) (run! visit x)\n1791\t                  (and (value-slot? d) (vector? x) (= :row (first x))) (visit (second x))\n1792\t                  :else nil)))]\n1793\t      (visit n)\n1794\t      @out)))\n1795\t\n1796\t\n1797\t(defn- task-tree\n1798\t  \"[task role] for the root and every install child, pre-order.\"\n1799\t  [task role]\n1800\t  (into [[task role]] (mapcat #(task-tree (nth (:slots %) 4) :child)) (nth (:slots task) 12)))\n1801\t\n1802\t\n1803\t(defn- check-stores!\n1804\t  \"Step 7's task context, beside X1: no root or module store key is a\n1805\t   reserved name (Rule R), refused here rather than by restore's store-put.\"\n1806\t  [_recv task _role]\n1807\t  (let [[_ _ _ _ _ _ store module-stores] (:slots task)]\n1808\t    (doseq [s (cons store (map #(second (:slots %)) module-stores))\n1809\t            k (take-nth 2 (:slots s))]\n1810\t      (when (vm/reserved-name? k)\n1811\t        (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :reserved-name {:yin.k/role :store-key :yin.k/name k})))))\n1812\t\n1813\t\n1814\t(defn- attaches?\n1815\t  \"The receiving kernel admits vector v (its loader's validation), under\n1816\t   address a when a is given.\"\n1817\t  [recv v a]\n1818\t  (try (let [r (module/attach-module recv v)] (or (nil? a) (contains? (:code-aliases r) a)))\n1819\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _e false)))"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72b4f199-a30e-42b5-b648-90d6dc2ab934","uuid":"4c5610eb-8623-4b1c-92a0-fad27426da3a","timestamp":"2026-10-13T13:59:56.939Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc","content":"(defn lift-task\n  \"The lift of §7.1: quiescent semantic-register machine m as a version-3\n   carrier, or a refusal thrown as ex-data {:yin.k/status :yin.k/kind}.\n   serve! is the exporter's remote-table entry (yin.vm.ucf.remote).\n   opts: :free-env, the task's initial free environment (default: the\n   kernel's retained :free-env field; the explicit value overrides it);\n   :source-index, {A #{tree-address}} the composition knows (§6.1), which\n   must cover every carried segment; :budget, the numbering budget;\n   :header, the exclusive custody header (occurrence, arbitration,\n   next-op-seq, origin when the task has a predecessor, and\n   :yin.k/enrolled, the enrolled stream identities, a lift input that\n   never travels); :serve-keyed, (f [task-path resource-id] handle), which\n   replaces serve! and is asked once per resource of each task, the task\n   path being the install names from the root ([] for the root itself),\n   so a caller can retain each answer under its key (holder.export's\n   record). No header is the fork: custody nil. A header writes the\n   root's slot by kind (header-custody), refuses :op-seq-exhausted at\n   2^52-1 on a blocked or parked root, and protects every retained write\n   of the tree (protect!). Before emitting, the lift runs custody-baseline\n   over the task, so it never emits a carrier the inspector refuses.\"\n  ([m serve!] (lift-task m serve! {}))\n  ([m serve! opts]\n   (let [opts (or opts {})\n         header (:header opts)\n         task (lift-task* m serve! opts :root)\n         kind (nth (:slots task) 2)\n         task (if (nil? header)\n                task\n                (let [n (:yin.k/next-op-seq header)]\n                  (when (and (not= :halted kind) (cbor/numeric? n) (cbor/num= n max-exact))\n                    (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :op-seq-exhausted {:yin.k/next-op-seq n}))\n                  (protect! task (or (:yin.k/enrolled header) #{}))\n                  (assoc-in task [:slots 16] (header-custody header kind))))]\n     (custody-baseline task)\n     (emit task (merge default-budget (:budget opts))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private fixed-resource-keys\n  #{vm/call-in-stream-key vm/call-out-stream-key vm/call-out-cursor-key\n    module/link-request-resource module/link-response-resource})\n\n\n(defn- fresh-key!\n  [used]\n  (loop [n (inc (count @used))]\n    (let [k (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"k-\" n))]\n      (if (contains? @used k) (recur (inc n)) (do (swap! used conj k) k)))))\n\n\n(defn- rows-of\n  \"Every row of kind under n; install children too unless own-only.\"\n  [n kind own-only?]\n  (let [out (atom [])]\n    (letfn [(visit\n              [n]\n              (when (= kind (:kind n)) (swap! out conj n))\n              (doseq [[d x] (map vector (descriptors (:kind n) (:slots n)) (:slots n))]\n                (cond\n                  (and (ref? d) (= :task (:kind x))) (when-not own-only? (visit x))\n                  (ref? d) (visit x)\n                  (refs? d) (run! visit x)\n                  (and (value-slot? d) (vector? x) (= :row (first x))) (visit (second x))\n                  :else nil)))]\n      (visit n)\n      @out)))\n\n\n(defn- task-tree\n  \"[task role] for the root and every install child, pre-order.\"\n  [task role]\n  (into [[task role]] (mapcat #(task-tree (nth (:slots %) 4) :child)) (nth (:slots task) 12)))\n\n\n(defn- check-stores!\n  \"Step 7's task context, beside X1: no root or module store key is a\n   reserved name (Rule R), refused here rather than by restore's store-put.\"\n  [_recv task _role]\n  (let [[_ _ _ _ _ _ store module-stores] (:slots task)]\n    (doseq [s (cons store (map #(second (:slots %)) module-stores))\n            k (take-nth 2 (:slots s))]\n      (when (vm/reserved-name? k)\n        (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :reserved-name {:yin.k/role :store-key :yin.k/name k})))))\n\n\n(defn- attaches?\n  \"The receiving kernel admits vector v (its loader's validation), under\n   address a when a is given.\"\n  [recv v a]\n  (try (let [r (module/attach-module recv v)] (or (nil? a) (contains? (:code-aliases r) a)))\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _e false)))","numLines":90,"startLine":1730,"totalLines":2263}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014eip4YzG8s7ArTH72Pz5Mi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
