{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016o3FMEE9CFdnbNXwhrW6xe","type":"tool_result","content":"1995\t         :yin.k/next-op-seq (:yin.k/next-op-seq c)\n1996\t         :protection classes :input {:next 0 :prefix prefix}\n1997\t         :tenure {:bound (:bound tenure)}}))))\n1998\t\n1999\t\n2000\t(defn- check-custody!\n2001\t  \"Step 10, once for the tree after the three staged checks: the custody\n2002\t   grammar (custody-baseline), then by the root's slot: a fork (nil) is\n2003\t   refused under :exclusive as :yin.k/profile-mismatch; an exclusive\n2004\t   blocked or parked root runs the grant checks unless :fenced (an\n2005\t   administrative rehydration: no grant, gate :exporting); a halted\n2006\t   exclusive root needs no grant and is gated :ended. Answers\n2007\t   {:exclusive? :fenced? :state}, which restore applies to every task.\"\n2008\t  [task wire opts]\n2009\t  (custody-baseline task)\n2010\t  (let [[_ _ kind] (:slots task) c (nth (:slots task) 16) fenced? (boolean (:fenced opts))]\n2011\t    (if (nil? c)\n2012\t      (do (when (:exclusive opts)\n2013\t            (outcome! :yin.k/profile-mismatch nil {:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive}))\n2014\t          {:exclusive? false :fenced? fenced?})\n2015\t      {:exclusive? true :fenced? fenced?\n2016\t       :state (when-not (or fenced? (= :halted kind)) (accept-grant! task c (pack-address wire) opts))})))\n2017\t\n2018\t\n2019\t(defn- with-custody\n2020\t  \"Restore's custody for one task of the tree: an exclusive tree numbers\n2021\t   its retained :put waits (:yin.k/issue, :yin.k/issued, in carried\n2022\t   order) and gates :running, a halted exclusive root :ended, the root\n2023\t   holding the grant's custody state; a fenced tree gates :exporting with\n2024\t   its waits and every parked record outside the scheduler\n2025\t   (:yin.k/recovery-waits, :yin.k/recovery-parked), the shape\n2026\t   holder.export's exporting machine has.\"\n2027\t  [m {:keys [exclusive? fenced? state]} kind root?]\n2028\t  (let [m (if exclusive?\n2029\t            (let [[entries issued] (reduce (fn [[acc i] e]\n2030\t                                             (if (= :put (:reason e))\n2031\t                                               [(conj acc (assoc e :yin.k/issue i)) (inc i)]\n2032\t                                               [(conj acc e) i]))\n2033\t                                           [[] 0] (:wait-set m))]\n2034\t              (cond-> (assoc m :wait-set entries :yin.k/issued issued\n2035\t                             :yin.k/gate (if (and root? (= :halted kind)) :ended :running))\n2036\t                (and root? (some? state)) (assoc :yin.k/custody state)))\n2037\t            m)]\n2038\t    (if fenced?\n2039\t      (assoc m :yin.k/gate :exporting :yin.k/recovery-waits (:wait-set m) :wait-set []\n2040\t             :yin.k/recovery-parked (:parked m) :parked {})\n2041\t      m)))\n2042\t\n2043\t\n2044\t(defn- attach-streams!\n2045\t  \"Step 11: one attach per distinct stream identity of the whole tree.\"\n2046\t  [attach! task]\n2047\t  (reduce (fn [acc s]\n2048\t            (let [[identity descriptor] (:slots s)]\n2049\t              (if (contains? acc identity)\n2050\t                acc\n2051\t                (if-some [h (remote/lower-marker attach! {:dao.stream/descriptor descriptor})]\n2052\t                  (assoc acc identity h)\n2053\t                  (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:dao.stream/identity identity})))))\n2054\t          {} (rows-of task :stream false)))\n2055\t\n2056\t\n2057\t(defn- spawn-child\n2058\t  \"A fresh install child of recv's composition (the engine's spawn\n2059\t   discipline): answers [child recv']. A fenced rehydration spawns it\n2060\t   without the stream constructor, so the child's construction creates no\n2061\t   stream (its default call pair): rehydration initializes nothing. The\n2062\t   constructor is the child's again afterwards.\"\n2063\t  [recv response mn fenced?]\n2064\t  (let [n (or (:origins recv) 0)\n2065\t        origin (keyword (str (name (or (:origin recv) :t0)) \".\" n))\n2066\t        registry (reduce (fn [r [m e]] (module/assoc-module r m (dissoc e :bindings)))\n2067\t                         (:modules recv) (module/module-entries (:modules recv)))\n2068\t        source (:secret-source recv)\n2069\t        child (module/spawn-module (cond-> recv fenced? (assoc :make-stream nil))\n2070\t                                   (:value (:image response))\n2071\t                                   {:modules registry :origin origin\n2072\t                                    :ancestry (conj (vec (:ancestry recv)) mn)\n2073\t                                    :capability-secret (when (fn? source) (source origin))})]\n2074\t    [(cond-> child fenced? (assoc :make-stream (:make-stream recv)))\n2075\t     (assoc recv :origins (inc n))]))\n2076\t\n2077\t\n2078\t(defn- restore-task\n2079\t  \"Step 12 for one task: code by A, fresh resource keys, values re-sealed\n2080\t   under recv, waits as engine entries, parked records, installs, and the\n2081\t   custody check-custody! answered (with-custody).\"\n2082\t  [recv task handles custody root?]\n2083\t  (let [[_ _ kind _ id-counter free-env store module-stores parked census _ code installs waits parked-id result]\n2084\t        (:slots task)\n2085\t        base (reduce (fn [r [_ v]] (module/attach-module r v))\n2086\t                     (assoc recv :code {} :code-aliases {} :program nil)\n2087\t                     (sort-by #(str (key %)) code))\n2088\t        aliases (:code-aliases base)\n2089\t        used (atom (into fixed-resource-keys (keys (:resources base))))\n2090\t        identities (sort-by str (distinct (map #(first (:slots %)) (rows-of task :stream true))))\n2091\t        stream-keys (into {} (map (fn [identity] [identity (fresh-key! used)])) identities)\n2092\t        pairs (mapv vec (partition 2 (:slots census)))\n2093\t        cell-keys (into {} (map (fn [[c _]] [c (fresh-key! used)])) pairs)\n2094\t        bodies (into {} pairs)\n2095\t        stream-key #(get stream-keys (first (:slots %)))\n2096\t        parked-index (into {} (map vec) (partition 2 (:slots parked)))\n2097\t        cache (atom {})\n2098\t        resolving (atom #{})]\n2099\t    (letfn [(value\n2100\t              [v]\n2101\t              (case (first v)\n2102\t                :lit (second v)\n2103\t                :cursor-cell (engine/issue-ref base :cursor-ref (get cell-keys (second v)))\n2104\t                :row (row (second v))))\n2105\t            (row\n2106\t              [n]\n2107\t              (let [ss (:slots n)]\n2108\t                (case (:kind n)\n2109\t                  :vec (mapv value ss)\n2110\t                  :list (apply list (map value ss))\n2111\t                  :set (into #{} (map value) ss)\n2112\t                  :map (into {} (map (fn [[k x]] [(value k) (value x)])) (partition 2 ss))\n2113\t                  :prim (vm/primitive-function (get (:primitives base) (first ss)))\n2114\t                  :stream (engine/issue-ref base :stream-ref (stream-key n))\n2115\t                  :closure (let [[a entry params bindings store-of] ss]\n2116\t                             (module/lower-closure base\n2117\t                                                   (cond-> {:yin.k/binding :named\n2118\t                                                            :yin.k/format :yin.semantic-register/code\n2119\t                                                            :yin.k/segment a :yin.k/entry entry :yin.k/params params\n2120\t                                                            :yin.k/env (keyed bindings)}\n2121\t                                                     (some? store-of) (assoc :yin.k/store-of store-of))\n2122\t                                                   identity))\n2123\t                  :reified (values/continuation (:owner base) (assoc (payload (first ss)) :type :reified-continuation))\n2124\t                  :parked-ref (parked-record (first ss)))))\n2125\t            (keyed\n2126\t              [n]\n2127\t              (into {} (map (fn [[k x]] [k (value x)])) (partition 2 (:slots n))))\n2128\t            (env\n2129\t              [n]\n2130\t              (let [[b store-of] (:slots n)]\n2131\t                (cond-> (keyed b) (some? store-of) (assoc engine/store-of-key store-of))))\n2132\t            (k-of\n2133\t              [n]\n2134\t              (mapv (fn [f]\n2135\t                      (let [[a pc e w rd] (:slots f)]\n2136\t                        {:type :return :segment (get aliases a) :pc pc :env (env e) :window (keyed w) :rd rd}))\n2137\t                    (:slots n)))\n2138\t            (payload\n2139\t              [n]\n2140\t              (if (= :tail (:kind n))\n2141\t                (let [[a site k] (:slots n)]\n2142\t                  {:segment (get aliases a) :site site :k (k-of k) :deliver {:deliver :return}})\n2143\t                (let [[a pc e w k rd] (:slots n)]\n2144\t                  {:segment (get aliases a) :pc pc :env (env e) :window (keyed w) :k (k-of k)\n2145\t                   :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd rd}})))\n2146\t            (parked-record\n2147\t              [p]\n2148\t              (or (get @cache p)\n2149\t                  (do (when (contains? @resolving p)\n2150\t                        (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :non-canonicalizable {:yin.k/hint :parked-cycle}))\n2151\t                      (swap! resolving conj p)\n2152\t                      (let [r (assoc (payload (get parked-index p)) :type :parked-continuation :id p)]\n2153\t                        (swap! cache assoc p r)\n2154\t                        (swap! resolving disj p)\n2155\t                        r))))\n2156\t            (cell-stream\n2157\t              [c]\n2158\t              (stream-key (first (:slots (get bodies c)))))\n2159\t            (entry\n2160\t              [w]\n2161\t              (let [[state pending] (:slots w)\n2162\t                    [reason & xs] (:slots pending)\n2163\t                    p (payload state)]\n2164\t                (case reason\n2165\t                  :next (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream (first xs))\n2166\t                               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys (first xs))})\n2167\t                  :ffi (let [[c call-id op] xs]\n2168\t                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream c) :call-id call-id\n2169\t                                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys c)})\n2170\t                           (some? op) (assoc :op op)))\n2171\t                  :put (let [[s v op-id] xs]\n2172\t                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key s) :datom (value v))\n2173\t                           (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n2174\t                  :ffi-request (let [[call-id envelope req resp c op-id] xs\n2175\t                                     datom (value envelope)]\n2176\t                                 (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key req) :datom datom\n2177\t                                                :request-sent true :call-id call-id :op (apply2/request-op datom)\n2178\t                                                :response-cursor (get cell-keys c) :response-stream (stream-key resp))\n2179\t                                   (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n2180\t                  (:link-request :link-response)\n2181\t                  (let [[link-id mn _ _ c envelope op-id] xs]\n2182\t                    (cond-> (assoc p :reason reason :link-id link-id :name mn\n2183\t                                   :request module/link-request-resource :response module/link-response-resource\n2184\t                                   :cursor (second (:slots (get bodies c))))\n2185\t                      (= :link-request reason) (assoc :envelope envelope)\n2186\t                      (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n2187\t                  :install (assoc p :reason :install :name (first xs)))))]\n2188\t      (let [store' (reduce (fn [s [k v]] (engine/store-put s k (value v))) {} (partition 2 (:slots store)))\n2189\t            stores (into {} (map (fn [ms]\n2190\t                                   (let [[mid s] (:slots ms)]\n2191\t                                     [mid (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (value v)])) (partition 2 (:slots s)))])))\n2192\t                         module-stores)\n2193\t            parked' (into {} (map (fn [[p _]] [p (parked-record p)])) parked-index)\n2194\t            entries (mapv entry waits)\n2195\t            link (some #(let [[reason _ _ req resp] (:slots (second (:slots %)))]\n2196\t                          (when (contains? #{:link-request :link-response} reason) [req resp]))\n2197\t                       waits)\n2198\t            [base installs'] (reduce (fn [[r acc] inst]\n2199\t                                       (let [[mn phase parent response child] (:slots inst)\n2200\t                                             [spawned r'] (spawn-child r response mn (:fenced? custody))]\n2201\t                                         [r' (assoc acc mn {:phase phase :parent parent :response response\n2202\t                                                            :vm (restore-task spawned child handles custody false)})]))\n2203\t                                     [base {}] installs)\n2204\t            fe (keyed free-env)\n2205\t            resources (merge (:resources base)\n2206\t                             (into {} (map (fn [[identity k]] [k (get handles identity)])) stream-keys)\n2207\t                             (into {} (map (fn [[c body]]\n2208\t                                             [(get cell-keys c) {:stream-id (stream-key (first (:slots body)))\n2209\t                                                                 :cursor (second (:slots body))}]))\n2210\t                                   pairs)\n2211\t                             (when-let [[req resp] link]\n2212\t                               {module/link-request-resource (get handles (first (:slots req)))\n2213\t                                module/link-response-resource (get handles (first (:slots resp)))}))\n2214\t            ;; a fenced rehydration carries the counter exactly, so the\n2215\t            ;; relift reproduces the published root; a resumption adopts\n2216\t            ;; max(local, carried)\n2217\t            machine (cond-> (assoc base :store store' :module-stores stores :parked parked' :installs installs'\n2218\t                                   :resources resources :env fe :free-env fe :window {} :k nil :control nil\n2219\t                                   :ready-queue []\n2220\t                                   :id-counter (if (:fenced? custody)\n2221\t                                                 id-counter\n2222\t                                                 (max (or (:id-counter base) 0) id-counter)))\n2223\t                      ;; resource key -> the carrier's cursor cell, so one\n2224\t                      ;; cell is one key and two cells two (UCF 7.7.4)\n2225\t                      (:fenced? custody)\n2226\t                      (assoc :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids (into {} (map (fn [[c k]] [k c])) cell-keys)))]\n2227\t        (with-custody\n2228\t          (case kind\n2229\t            :halted (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (value result) :wait-set [])\n2230\t            :parked (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (get parked' parked-id) :wait-set entries)\n2231\t            (assoc machine :halted? false :blocked? true :value :yin/blocked :wait-set entries))\n2232\t          custody kind root?)))))\n2233\t\n2234\t\n2235\t(defn lower-task\n2236\t  \"The lower of §7.2 into recv, a fresh semantic-register machine of the\n2237\t   receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,\n2238\t   then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,\n2239\t   primitives), each step over the whole tree before the next, then\n2240\t   custody (check-custody!), all before the first attach! (step 11); then\n2241\t   restore (step 12), which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the\n2242\t   restored machine, or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\n2243\t   opts: :budget; :exclusive, refuse a fork root; :grant and :protection,\n2244\t   required by a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's reader\n2245\t   contract: the grant names :checkpoint, the pack address, its lease,\n2246\t   holder, tenure and evidence; :protection maps every stream identity of\n2247\t   the tree to its class); :fenced, an administrative rehydration that\n2248\t   skips the grant and restores every task of the tree gated :exporting,\n2249\t   its waits in :yin.k/recovery-waits and its parked records in\n2250\t   :yin.k/recovery-parked (none in the scheduler), its id counter the\n2251\t   carried one exactly and :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids mapping each cursor\n2252\t   cell's resource key to its carried cell id.\"\n2253\t  ([recv wire attach!] (lower-task recv wire attach! {}))\n2254\t  ([recv wire attach! opts]\n2255\t   (let [task (decode wire (merge default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n2256\t     (when-not (= :task (:kind task)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :root {}))\n2257\t     ;; each step over the whole tree before the next (§3.3)\n2258\t     (doseq [step [check-stores! check-pendings! check-dependencies!]\n2259\t             [t role] (task-tree task :root)]\n2260\t       (step recv t role))\n2261\t     (let [custody (check-custody! task wire opts)]\n2262\t       (restore-task recv task (attach-streams! attach! task) custody true)))))\n2263\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72b4f199-a30e-42b5-b648-90d6dc2ab934","uuid":"c8df427c-6c60-4b33-b03e-d6aadcbb500d","timestamp":"2026-10-13T13:59:57.607Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc","content":"         :yin.k/next-op-seq (:yin.k/next-op-seq c)\n         :protection classes :input {:next 0 :prefix prefix}\n         :tenure {:bound (:bound tenure)}}))))\n\n\n(defn- check-custody!\n  \"Step 10, once for the tree after the three staged checks: the custody\n   grammar (custody-baseline), then by the root's slot: a fork (nil) is\n   refused under :exclusive as :yin.k/profile-mismatch; an exclusive\n   blocked or parked root runs the grant checks unless :fenced (an\n   administrative rehydration: no grant, gate :exporting); a halted\n   exclusive root needs no grant and is gated :ended. Answers\n   {:exclusive? :fenced? :state}, which restore applies to every task.\"\n  [task wire opts]\n  (custody-baseline task)\n  (let [[_ _ kind] (:slots task) c (nth (:slots task) 16) fenced? (boolean (:fenced opts))]\n    (if (nil? c)\n      (do (when (:exclusive opts)\n            (outcome! :yin.k/profile-mismatch nil {:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive}))\n          {:exclusive? false :fenced? fenced?})\n      {:exclusive? true :fenced? fenced?\n       :state (when-not (or fenced? (= :halted kind)) (accept-grant! task c (pack-address wire) opts))})))\n\n\n(defn- with-custody\n  \"Restore's custody for one task of the tree: an exclusive tree numbers\n   its retained :put waits (:yin.k/issue, :yin.k/issued, in carried\n   order) and gates :running, a halted exclusive root :ended, the root\n   holding the grant's custody state; a fenced tree gates :exporting with\n   its waits and every parked record outside the scheduler\n   (:yin.k/recovery-waits, :yin.k/recovery-parked), the shape\n   holder.export's exporting machine has.\"\n  [m {:keys [exclusive? fenced? state]} kind root?]\n  (let [m (if exclusive?\n            (let [[entries issued] (reduce (fn [[acc i] e]\n                                             (if (= :put (:reason e))\n                                               [(conj acc (assoc e :yin.k/issue i)) (inc i)]\n                                               [(conj acc e) i]))\n                                           [[] 0] (:wait-set m))]\n              (cond-> (assoc m :wait-set entries :yin.k/issued issued\n                             :yin.k/gate (if (and root? (= :halted kind)) :ended :running))\n                (and root? (some? state)) (assoc :yin.k/custody state)))\n            m)]\n    (if fenced?\n      (assoc m :yin.k/gate :exporting :yin.k/recovery-waits (:wait-set m) :wait-set []\n             :yin.k/recovery-parked (:parked m) :parked {})\n      m)))\n\n\n(defn- attach-streams!\n  \"Step 11: one attach per distinct stream identity of the whole tree.\"\n  [attach! task]\n  (reduce (fn [acc s]\n            (let [[identity descriptor] (:slots s)]\n              (if (contains? acc identity)\n                acc\n                (if-some [h (remote/lower-marker attach! {:dao.stream/descriptor descriptor})]\n                  (assoc acc identity h)\n                  (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:dao.stream/identity identity})))))\n          {} (rows-of task :stream false)))\n\n\n(defn- spawn-child\n  \"A fresh install child of recv's composition (the engine's spawn\n   discipline): answers [child recv']. A fenced rehydration spawns it\n   without the stream constructor, so the child's construction creates no\n   stream (its default call pair): rehydration initializes nothing. The\n   constructor is the child's again afterwards.\"\n  [recv response mn fenced?]\n  (let [n (or (:origins recv) 0)\n        origin (keyword (str (name (or (:origin recv) :t0)) \".\" n))\n        registry (reduce (fn [r [m e]] (module/assoc-module r m (dissoc e :bindings)))\n                         (:modules recv) (module/module-entries (:modules recv)))\n        source (:secret-source recv)\n        child (module/spawn-module (cond-> recv fenced? (assoc :make-stream nil))\n                                   (:value (:image response))\n                                   {:modules registry :origin origin\n                                    :ancestry (conj (vec (:ancestry recv)) mn)\n                                    :capability-secret (when (fn? source) (source origin))})]\n    [(cond-> child fenced? (assoc :make-stream (:make-stream recv)))\n     (assoc recv :origins (inc n))]))\n\n\n(defn- restore-task\n  \"Step 12 for one task: code by A, fresh resource keys, values re-sealed\n   under recv, waits as engine entries, parked records, installs, and the\n   custody check-custody! answered (with-custody).\"\n  [recv task handles custody root?]\n  (let [[_ _ kind _ id-counter free-env store module-stores parked census _ code installs waits parked-id result]\n        (:slots task)\n        base (reduce (fn [r [_ v]] (module/attach-module r v))\n                     (assoc recv :code {} :code-aliases {} :program nil)\n                     (sort-by #(str (key %)) code))\n        aliases (:code-aliases base)\n        used (atom (into fixed-resource-keys (keys (:resources base))))\n        identities (sort-by str (distinct (map #(first (:slots %)) (rows-of task :stream true))))\n        stream-keys (into {} (map (fn [identity] [identity (fresh-key! used)])) identities)\n        pairs (mapv vec (partition 2 (:slots census)))\n        cell-keys (into {} (map (fn [[c _]] [c (fresh-key! used)])) pairs)\n        bodies (into {} pairs)\n        stream-key #(get stream-keys (first (:slots %)))\n        parked-index (into {} (map vec) (partition 2 (:slots parked)))\n        cache (atom {})\n        resolving (atom #{})]\n    (letfn [(value\n              [v]\n              (case (first v)\n                :lit (second v)\n                :cursor-cell (engine/issue-ref base :cursor-ref (get cell-keys (second v)))\n                :row (row (second v))))\n            (row\n              [n]\n              (let [ss (:slots n)]\n                (case (:kind n)\n                  :vec (mapv value ss)\n                  :list (apply list (map value ss))\n                  :set (into #{} (map value) ss)\n                  :map (into {} (map (fn [[k x]] [(value k) (value x)])) (partition 2 ss))\n                  :prim (vm/primitive-function (get (:primitives base) (first ss)))\n                  :stream (engine/issue-ref base :stream-ref (stream-key n))\n                  :closure (let [[a entry params bindings store-of] ss]\n                             (module/lower-closure base\n                                                   (cond-> {:yin.k/binding :named\n                                                            :yin.k/format :yin.semantic-register/code\n                                                            :yin.k/segment a :yin.k/entry entry :yin.k/params params\n                                                            :yin.k/env (keyed bindings)}\n                                                     (some? store-of) (assoc :yin.k/store-of store-of))\n                                                   identity))\n                  :reified (values/continuation (:owner base) (assoc (payload (first ss)) :type :reified-continuation))\n                  :parked-ref (parked-record (first ss)))))\n            (keyed\n              [n]\n              (into {} (map (fn [[k x]] [k (value x)])) (partition 2 (:slots n))))\n            (env\n              [n]\n              (let [[b store-of] (:slots n)]\n                (cond-> (keyed b) (some? store-of) (assoc engine/store-of-key store-of))))\n            (k-of\n              [n]\n              (mapv (fn [f]\n                      (let [[a pc e w rd] (:slots f)]\n                        {:type :return :segment (get aliases a) :pc pc :env (env e) :window (keyed w) :rd rd}))\n                    (:slots n)))\n            (payload\n              [n]\n              (if (= :tail (:kind n))\n                (let [[a site k] (:slots n)]\n                  {:segment (get aliases a) :site site :k (k-of k) :deliver {:deliver :return}})\n                (let [[a pc e w k rd] (:slots n)]\n                  {:segment (get aliases a) :pc pc :env (env e) :window (keyed w) :k (k-of k)\n                   :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd rd}})))\n            (parked-record\n              [p]\n              (or (get @cache p)\n                  (do (when (contains? @resolving p)\n                        (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :non-canonicalizable {:yin.k/hint :parked-cycle}))\n                      (swap! resolving conj p)\n                      (let [r (assoc (payload (get parked-index p)) :type :parked-continuation :id p)]\n                        (swap! cache assoc p r)\n                        (swap! resolving disj p)\n                        r))))\n            (cell-stream\n              [c]\n              (stream-key (first (:slots (get bodies c)))))\n            (entry\n              [w]\n              (let [[state pending] (:slots w)\n                    [reason & xs] (:slots pending)\n                    p (payload state)]\n                (case reason\n                  :next (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream (first xs))\n                               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys (first xs))})\n                  :ffi (let [[c call-id op] xs]\n                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream c) :call-id call-id\n                                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys c)})\n                           (some? op) (assoc :op op)))\n                  :put (let [[s v op-id] xs]\n                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key s) :datom (value v))\n                           (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n                  :ffi-request (let [[call-id envelope req resp c op-id] xs\n                                     datom (value envelope)]\n                                 (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key req) :datom datom\n                                                :request-sent true :call-id call-id :op (apply2/request-op datom)\n                                                :response-cursor (get cell-keys c) :response-stream (stream-key resp))\n                                   (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n                  (:link-request :link-response)\n                  (let [[link-id mn _ _ c envelope op-id] xs]\n                    (cond-> (assoc p :reason reason :link-id link-id :name mn\n                                   :request module/link-request-resource :response module/link-response-resource\n                                   :cursor (second (:slots (get bodies c))))\n                      (= :link-request reason) (assoc :envelope envelope)\n                      (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n                  :install (assoc p :reason :install :name (first xs)))))]\n      (let [store' (reduce (fn [s [k v]] (engine/store-put s k (value v))) {} (partition 2 (:slots store)))\n            stores (into {} (map (fn [ms]\n                                   (let [[mid s] (:slots ms)]\n                                     [mid (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (value v)])) (partition 2 (:slots s)))])))\n                         module-stores)\n            parked' (into {} (map (fn [[p _]] [p (parked-record p)])) parked-index)\n            entries (mapv entry waits)\n            link (some #(let [[reason _ _ req resp] (:slots (second (:slots %)))]\n                          (when (contains? #{:link-request :link-response} reason) [req resp]))\n                       waits)\n            [base installs'] (reduce (fn [[r acc] inst]\n                                       (let [[mn phase parent response child] (:slots inst)\n                                             [spawned r'] (spawn-child r response mn (:fenced? custody))]\n                                         [r' (assoc acc mn {:phase phase :parent parent :response response\n                                                            :vm (restore-task spawned child handles custody false)})]))\n                                     [base {}] installs)\n            fe (keyed free-env)\n            resources (merge (:resources base)\n                             (into {} (map (fn [[identity k]] [k (get handles identity)])) stream-keys)\n                             (into {} (map (fn [[c body]]\n                                             [(get cell-keys c) {:stream-id (stream-key (first (:slots body)))\n                                                                 :cursor (second (:slots body))}]))\n                                   pairs)\n                             (when-let [[req resp] link]\n                               {module/link-request-resource (get handles (first (:slots req)))\n                                module/link-response-resource (get handles (first (:slots resp)))}))\n            ;; a fenced rehydration carries the counter exactly, so the\n            ;; relift reproduces the published root; a resumption adopts\n            ;; max(local, carried)\n            machine (cond-> (assoc base :store store' :module-stores stores :parked parked' :installs installs'\n                                   :resources resources :env fe :free-env fe :window {} :k nil :control nil\n                                   :ready-queue []\n                                   :id-counter (if (:fenced? custody)\n                                                 id-counter\n                                                 (max (or (:id-counter base) 0) id-counter)))\n                      ;; resource key -> the carrier's cursor cell, so one\n                      ;; cell is one key and two cells two (UCF 7.7.4)\n                      (:fenced? custody)\n                      (assoc :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids (into {} (map (fn [[c k]] [k c])) cell-keys)))]\n        (with-custody\n          (case kind\n            :halted (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (value result) :wait-set [])\n            :parked (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (get parked' parked-id) :wait-set entries)\n            (assoc machine :halted? false :blocked? true :value :yin/blocked :wait-set entries))\n          custody kind root?)))))\n\n\n(defn lower-task\n  \"The lower of §7.2 into recv, a fresh semantic-register machine of the\n   receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,\n   then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,\n   primitives), each step over the whole tree before the next, then\n   custody (check-custody!), all before the first attach! (step 11); then\n   restore (step 12), which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the\n   restored machine, or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\n   opts: :budget; :exclusive, refuse a fork root; :grant and :protection,\n   required by a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's reader\n   contract: the grant names :checkpoint, the pack address, its lease,\n   holder, tenure and evidence; :protection maps every stream identity of\n   the tree to its class); :fenced, an administrative rehydration that\n   skips the grant and restores every task of the tree gated :exporting,\n   its waits in :yin.k/recovery-waits and its parked records in\n   :yin.k/recovery-parked (none in the scheduler), its id counter the\n   carried one exactly and :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids mapping each cursor\n   cell's resource key to its carried cell id.\"\n  ([recv wire attach!] (lower-task recv wire attach! {}))\n  ([recv wire attach! opts]\n   (let [task (decode wire (merge default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n     (when-not (= :task (:kind task)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :root {}))\n     ;; each step over the whole tree before the next (§3.3)\n     (doseq [step [check-stores! check-pendings! check-dependencies!]\n             [t role] (task-tree task :root)]\n       (step recv t role))\n     (let [custody (check-custody! task wire opts)]\n       (restore-task recv task (attach-streams! attach! task) custody true)))))\n"