{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JsTKPgf66mGPg33Lg978Vb","type":"tool_result","content":"40\t(def lowering-profile\n41\t  \"The lowering profile this repository implements, exactly as published\n42\t   in §5.2.1: `\\\"ast-to-bytecode\\\"` over the UCF §7.3.3 stamp\n43\t   `{:yin.code/contract \\\"v3\\\", :yin.k/version 0}`\n44\t   (`vm/semantic-contract`). A `:derive` record\n45\t   carries this map verbatim, and `verify-derivation` recomputes a\n46\t   derivation only when the record's profile is `=` to the profile the\n47\t   consumer implements (§5.2.2 step 2).\"\n48\t  {:yin.lower/profile \"ast-to-bytecode\"\n49\t   :yin.code/contract vm/semantic-contract\n50\t   :yin.k/version 0})\n51\t\n52\t\n53\t(defn derive-record\n54\t  \"§5.2/§8.2's `:derive` record: `output` was computed from `input` by\n55\t   `:yin.vm/lower` under `lowering-profile`. A plain map, so it is\n56\t   content-addressed by `dao.jing/segment-key`, immutable, and\n57\t   verifiable; its own address is what the ledger publishes. The\n58\t   addresses are the only coordinates — the record holds no log-local\n59\t   id, so it is hashed once, when built.\"\n60\t  [input output]\n61\t  {:yin.ledger/op :derive\n62\t   :yin.ledger/input input\n63\t   :yin.ledger/output output\n64\t   :yin.ledger/function :yin.vm/lower\n65\t   :yin.ledger/profile lowering-profile})\n66\t\n67\t\n68\t(defn derive-event\n69\t  \"§8.2's ledger event tx-data for one record: a local entity with the\n70\t   record's fields as attributes and the record's address as one more.\n71\t   `ev` is a tempid — distinct tempids for distinct events, whether in\n72\t   one transaction or several. The profile travels as the structured map,\n73\t   exactly as it appears in the record; no string rendering is defined.\"\n74\t  [ev {:yin.ledger/keys [op input output function profile] :as record}]\n75\t  [[:db/add ev :yin.ledger/op op]\n76\t   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/input input]\n77\t   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/output output]\n78\t   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/function function]\n79\t   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/profile profile]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72b4f199-a30e-42b5-b648-90d6dc2ab934","uuid":"ad51bfaa-415e-4565-be21-33ab20e947e6","timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:00:28.435Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b/src/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc","content":"(def lowering-profile\n  \"The lowering profile this repository implements, exactly as published\n   in §5.2.1: `\\\"ast-to-bytecode\\\"` over the UCF §7.3.3 stamp\n   `{:yin.code/contract \\\"v3\\\", :yin.k/version 0}`\n   (`vm/semantic-contract`). A `:derive` record\n   carries this map verbatim, and `verify-derivation` recomputes a\n   derivation only when the record's profile is `=` to the profile the\n   consumer implements (§5.2.2 step 2).\"\n  {:yin.lower/profile \"ast-to-bytecode\"\n   :yin.code/contract vm/semantic-contract\n   :yin.k/version 0})\n\n\n(defn derive-record\n  \"§5.2/§8.2's `:derive` record: `output` was computed from `input` by\n   `:yin.vm/lower` under `lowering-profile`. A plain map, so it is\n   content-addressed by `dao.jing/segment-key`, immutable, and\n   verifiable; its own address is what the ledger publishes. The\n   addresses are the only coordinates — the record holds no log-local\n   id, so it is hashed once, when built.\"\n  [input output]\n  {:yin.ledger/op :derive\n   :yin.ledger/input input\n   :yin.ledger/output output\n   :yin.ledger/function :yin.vm/lower\n   :yin.ledger/profile lowering-profile})\n\n\n(defn derive-event\n  \"§8.2's ledger event tx-data for one record: a local entity with the\n   record's fields as attributes and the record's address as one more.\n   `ev` is a tempid — distinct tempids for distinct events, whether in\n   one transaction or several. The profile travels as the structured map,\n   exactly as it appears in the record; no string rendering is defined.\"\n  [ev {:yin.ledger/keys [op input output function profile] :as record}]\n  [[:db/add ev :yin.ledger/op op]\n   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/input input]\n   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/output output]\n   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/function function]\n   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/profile profile]","numLines":40,"startLine":40,"totalLines":272}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JsTKPgf66mGPg33Lg978Vb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
