:tree tree, :trust :verified}]\n2236\t              (let [actual (relowered format-kw tree)]\n2237\t                (cond\n2238\t                  (nil? actual)\n2239\t                  [state (refused :unverified-derivation\n2240\t                                  {:format format-kw, :profile profile,\n2241\t                                   :missing :relowering})]\n2242\t\n2243\t                  (not= output actual)\n2244\t                  [state (refused :derivation-mismatch\n2245\t                                  {:format format-kw, :output output,\n2246\t                                   :actual actual})]\n2247\t\n2248\t                  :else [state {:derivation derivation, :output output,\n2249\t                                :tree tree, :trust :verified}])))))))))\n2250\t\n2251\t\n2252\t(defn- checked-derivation\n2253\t  \"The derivation half of a manifest link (section 8.1): fetch the\n2254\t   format's record through `record-format`, check its two addresses --\n2255\t   the record's input is the manifest's tree, its output is the identity\n2256\t   the image is then fetched at -- and apply the policy, `:trusted`\n2257\t   stopping at the addresses, `:verifying` recomputing. Returns `[state\n2258\t   outcome]`, the outcome of `verified-policy-outcome`'s shape with\n2259\t   `:trust :composition` under `:trusted`, or a refusal. A manifest\n2260\t   with no record for the format is `:unsupported-format`.\"\n2261\t  [state drive format-kw manifest policy]\n2262\t  (let [tree-addr (:yin.module/tree manifest)\n2263\t        derivation-addr (get (:yin.module/derivations manifest) format-kw)]\n2264\t    (if (nil? derivation-addr)\n2265\t      [state (refused :unsupported-format {:format format-kw})]\n2266\t      (let [[state c] (drive-link state drive :yin.ledger/record\n2267\t                                  derivation-addr\n2268\t                                  (:contract record-format))]\n2269\t        (if (refused? c)\n2270\t          [state (dissoc c :yin.link/id)]\n2271\t          (let [derivation (get-in c [:image :value])]\n2272\t            (if (not= tree-addr (:yin.ledger/input derivation))\n2273\t              [state (refused :derivation-mismatch\n2274\t                              {:format format-kw, :expected tree-addr,\n2275\t                               :actual (:yin.ledger/input derivation)})]\n2276\t              (if (= :trusted policy)\n2277\t                [state {:derivation derivation,\n2278\t                        :output (:yin.ledger/output derivation),\n2279\t                        :trust :composition}]\n2280\t                (verified-policy-outcome state drive format-kw derivation\n2281\t                                         tree-addr)))))))))\n2282\t\n2283\t\n2284\t(defn- linked-image\n2285\t  \"The image half of a manifest link (section 8.1): fetch the image at\n2286\t   `identity` through the format record -- the six steps, obligations\n2287\t   included -- verify the semantic derivation against the fetched image\n2288\t   when the `:verifying` policy fetched the tree (`yin.vm.ledger`'s own\n2289\t   content-and-derivation check; the de Bruijn formats' recomputation\n2290\t   ran before the image, needing none), join every retained obligation\n2291\t   with the manifest's declarations, and discharge against `receiver` --\n2292\t   unless `defer?`, the serving composition's choice (section 7.2 steps 6\n2293\t   and 7): the obligations then travel for the receiving task's own step\n2294\t   5b, which runs against its live state. `derivation` is"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72b4f199-a30e-42b5-b648-90d6dc2ab934","uuid":"092f7a74-4907-4e85-864d-422e176e91f7","timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:01:00.251Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc","content":"\n(defn- verified-policy-outcome\n  \"The `:verifying` policy's checks once the record's addresses hold\n   (section 8.1): the profile the record names must be the one this\n   linker implements for the format; the manifest's tree is fetched and\n   verified through `ast-format` at steps 2 to 4 and no further -- its\n   obligations are the walker's, scanned only when the tree is the\n   requested image; and the two de Bruijn formats'\n   recomputed identity must equal the record's output. The semantic\n   format's recomputation runs in `linked-image`, against the fetched\n   image, through `yin.vm.ledger`'s own check. Returns `[state\n   outcome]`, the outcome `{:derivation r :output o :tree t :trust\n   :verified}` or a refusal.\"\n  [state drive format-kw derivation tree-addr]\n  (let [profile (:yin.ledger/profile derivation)\n        implemented (get implemented-profiles format-kw)]\n    (if (not= profile implemented)\n      [state (refused :unverified-derivation\n                      {:format format-kw, :profile profile,\n                       :implemented implemented, :missing :profile})]\n      (let [[state tc] (drive-link state drive :yin.ast/code tree-addr\n                                   vm/ast-contract false)]\n        (if (refused? tc)\n          [state (refused :unverified-derivation\n                          {:format format-kw, :profile profile,\n                           :missing (:reason tc)})]\n          (let [tree (get-in tc [:image :value])\n                output (:yin.ledger/output derivation)]\n            (if (= :yin.semantic/code format-kw)\n              [state {:derivation derivation, :output output,\n                      :tree tree, :trust :verified}]\n              (let [actual (relowered format-kw tree)]\n                (cond\n                  (nil? actual)\n                  [state (refused :unverified-derivation\n                                  {:format format-kw, :profile profile,\n                                   :missing :relowering})]\n\n                  (not= output actual)\n                  [state (refused :derivation-mismatch\n                                  {:format format-kw, :output output,\n                                   :actual actual})]\n\n                  :else [state {:derivation derivation, :output output,\n                                :tree tree, :trust :verified}])))))))))\n\n\n(defn- checked-derivation\n  \"The derivation half of a manifest link (section 8.1): fetch the\n   format's record through `record-format`, check its two addresses --\n   the record's input is the manifest's tree, its output is the identity\n   the image is then fetched at -- and apply the policy, `:trusted`\n   stopping at the addresses, `:verifying` recomputing. Returns `[state\n   outcome]`, the outcome of `verified-policy-outcome`'s shape with\n   `:trust :composition` under `:trusted`, or a refusal. A manifest\n   with no record for the format is `:unsupported-format`.\"\n  [state drive format-kw manifest policy]\n  (let [tree-addr (:yin.module/tree manifest)\n        derivation-addr (get (:yin.module/derivations manifest) format-kw)]\n    (if (nil? derivation-addr)\n      [state (refused :unsupported-format {:format format-kw})]\n      (let [[state c] (drive-link state drive :yin.ledger/record\n                                  derivation-addr\n                                  (:contract record-format))]\n        (if (refused? c)\n          [state (dissoc c :yin.link/id)]\n          (let [derivation (get-in c [:image :value])]\n            (if (not= tree-addr (:yin.ledger/input derivation))\n              [state (refused :derivation-mismatch\n                              {:format format-kw, :expected tree-addr,\n                               :actual (:yin.ledger/input derivation)})]\n              (if (= :trusted policy)\n                [state {:derivation derivation,\n                        :output (:yin.ledger/output derivation),\n                        :trust :composition}]\n                (verified-policy-outcome state drive format-kw derivation\n                                         tree-addr)))))))))\n\n\n(defn- linked-image\n  \"The image half of a manifest link (section 8.1): fetch the image at\n   `identity` through the format record -- the six steps, obligations\n   included -- verify the semantic derivation against the fetched image\n   when the `:verifying` policy fetched the tree (`yin.vm.ledger`'s own\n   content-and-derivation check; the de Bruijn formats' recomputation\n   ran before the image, needing none), join every retained obligation\n   with the manifest's declarations, and discharge against `receiver` --\n   unless `defer?`, the serving composition's choice (section 7.2 steps 6\n   and 7): the obligations then travel for the receiving task's own step\n   5b, which runs against its live state. `derivation` is","numLines":90,"startLine":2205,"totalLines":2566}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KfEbMHZerSBe97AAWpnSaS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
