{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T2i59qftJdnTujEebrMaDU","type":"tool_result","content":"2295\t   `checked-derivation`'s outcome, nil for the tree format. Returns\n2296\t   `[state outcome]`, `fetch`'s outcome shape plus `:manifest` and, for a\n2297\t   lowered format, `:derivation` and `:trust`.\"\n2298\t  [state drive record identity manifest derivation receiver defer?]\n2299\t  (let [[state c] (drive-link state drive (:format record) identity\n2300\t                              (:contract record))]\n2301\t    (if (refused? c)\n2302\t      [state (dissoc c :yin.link/id)]\n2303\t      (if-let [verdict\n2304\t               (and (= :yin.semantic/code (:format record))\n2305\t                    (:tree derivation)\n2306\t                    (ledger/verify-derivation\n2307\t                      (:tree derivation)\n2308\t                      (get-in c [:image :value])\n2309\t                      (:derivation derivation)\n2310\t                      (get implemented-profiles :yin.semantic/code)))]\n2311\t        [state (refused (if (= :yin.k/profile-mismatch (:kind verdict))\n2312\t                          :unverified-derivation\n2313\t                          :derivation-mismatch)\n2314\t                        (assoc verdict :format (:format record)))]\n2315\t        (let [declared (manifest-join manifest (:obligations c))]\n2316\t          (if (refused? declared)\n2317\t            [state declared]\n2318\t            (let [outcome (merge {:status :ok}\n2319\t                                 (:image c)\n2320\t                                 {:obligations declared,\n2321\t                                  :manifest manifest}\n2322\t                                 (when (:derivation derivation)\n2323\t                                   {:derivation (:derivation derivation),\n2324\t                                    :trust (:trust derivation)}))]\n2325\t              [state (if defer?\n2326\t                       outcome\n2327\t                       (or (discharge receiver declared) outcome))])))))))\n2328\t\n2329\t\n2330\t(defn link-manifest\n2331\t  \"Link one format's image through a module manifest (section 8.1): the\n2332\t   manifest-delivered image flow of section 7.2 step 5, as host policy\n2333\t   over a link runtime. `manifest-address` is the manifest's own content\n2334\t   address -- the composition resolved the name itself, through its\n2335\t   name environment or the section 8.2 authority policy, and names the\n2336\t   resolution in `opts` as `:name`. `receiver` is `fetch`'s receiver.\n2337\t   `opts` carries the requester's `:contract` (required), the\n2338\t   `:derivation` policy (`:verifying`, the default, or `:trusted`), the\n2339\t   resolution `:name`, and `:defer-discharge`: a serving composition\n2340\t   (section 7.2) sets it true, and step 8 -- the linker-side 5b -- is\n2341\t   skipped, the obligations travelling for the receiving task's own step\n2342\t   5b against its live state (section 7.2, step 7).\n2343\t\n2344\t   The order is fixed (sections 4.2 and 8.1):\n2345\t     0. the format record; the requester's contract    :unsupported-format,\n2346\t        against it                                     :contract-mismatch\n2347\t     1. the manifest fetch: steps 1 to 4 through        :absent,\n2348\t        `manifest-format`, so the manifest itself is   :address-mismatch,\n2349\t        verified content                              :descriptor-defect\n2350\t     2. the manifest's contract entry for the format    :contract-mismatch\n2351\t        against the format record's, before the name\n2352\t        check and before any derivation or image\n2353\t     3. `:yin.module/name` against `opts`'s `:name`     :module-name-mismatch\n2354\t     4. the derivation record fetch and its two         :unsupported-format,\n2355\t        address checks: input = the manifest's tree,   :derivation-mismatch\n2356\t        output = the identity the image is fetched at\n2357\t     5. under `:verifying`: the profile is implemented, :unverified-derivation,\n2358\t        the tree is verified content, and the          :derivation-mismatch\n2359\t        recomputed identity is the record's output;\n2360\t        under `:trusted` the addresses are everything\n2361\t     6. the image fetch: the six steps through the      fetch's refusals\n2362\t        format record\n2363\t     7. every retained obligation is declared           :undeclared-free\n2364\t     8. discharge (5b) against `receiver`, unless       :unresolved-free,\n2365\t        `:defer-discharge`                              :shadowed-free\n2366\t\n2367\t   The manifest's `:yin.module/index` is merged into the linker-local\n2368\t   index of the requested format the moment the manifest is verified.\n2369\t   The outcome is `fetch`'s plus `:manifest`, and for a lowered format\n2370\t   `:derivation` and `:trust` (`:verified` or `:composition`: a trusted\n2371\t   link never reports a verification it did not perform). The tree\n2372\t   format needs no derivation under either policy; it is the tree,\n2373\t   verified by content. No contract stamp is ever assigned to external\n2374\t   input.\"\n2375\t  ([runtime manifest-address format-kw receiver]\n2376\t   (link-manifest runtime manifest-address format-kw receiver nil))\n2377\t  ([runtime manifest-address format-kw receiver opts]\n2378\t   (let [{:keys [state drive]} runtime\n2379\t         record (get (:formats state) format-kw)\n2380\t         contract (:contract opts)\n2381\t         policy (or (:derivation opts) :verifying)\n2382\t         defer? (boolean (:defer-discharge opts))]\n2383\t     (cond\n2384\t       (nil? record)\n2385\t       (refused :unsupported-format {:format format-kw})\n2386\t\n2387\t       (nil? contract)\n2388\t       (refused :invalid-request {:missing :contract})\n2389\t\n2390\t       (not= contract (:contract record))\n2391\t       (refused :contract-mismatch\n2392\t                {:expected