{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L6VXy3gV2NqMnxvK9DkUM3","type":"tool_result","content":"2086\t(defn check-wait-set\n2087\t  \"Check wait-set entries against their transports.\n2088\t\n2089\t   The sweep is `dao.stream.waitset/check` — this engine was that library's\n2090\t   seed and is now its first consumer. Every entry is resolved to a live\n2091\t   handle and an opaque cursor out of the store by `waitset-resolver` and\n2092\t   polled with a synchronous `next` or `append!` — resolution happens per\n2093\t   poll, so the stored entry itself never carries a handle. There is no\n2094\t   transport-local waking to fall back from: this is the only mechanism.\n2095\t\n2096\t   Entries are polled one at a time in wait-set order, and a woken reader's\n2097\t   successor cursor is written back to the store before the next entry is\n2098\t   resolved. Waiters sharing a cursor-ref therefore read distinct values —\n2099\t   the value at the cursor wakes the first, its successor wakes the next —\n2100\t   instead of every waiter reading the value at the shared pre-poll\n2101\t   cursor. An entry that stays waiting is retained in its stored,\n2102\t   resource-id form.\n2103\t\n2104\t   Each woken result's `:status` is stamped onto its ready entry, where\n2105\t   `terminal-resume-outcome` reads it: an outcome the immediate operation\n2106\t   raises as an error fails the same way when the resume pops it — and a\n2107\t   waitset diagnostic, an entry the sweep could not poll at all, raises\n2108\t   there too, before any continuation is restored.\n2109\t\n2110\t   The link wait entries `require` adds (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.2) are\n2111\t   polled first, by the engine rather than the stream sweep: a\n2112\t   `:link-request` retries its envelope, a `:link-response` advances its\n2113\t   own kept cursor to the response carrying its id, and an `:install`\n2114\t   waits on its install child. The install children are then stepped in\n2115\t   this same round (section 7.3), so a child that halts restores its\n2116\t   waiters here; nothing about a child runs inside a restore.\n2117\t\n2118\t   The FFI response readers are routed next, also outside the stream\n2119\t   sweep (`poll-ffi-responses`): a response wakes the reader whose call\n2120\t   id it names, never whichever reader its cell reached first.\n2121\t\n2122\t   A gated machine (any `:yin.k/gate`) observes nothing here: no link\n2123\t   retry or scan, no FFI response read, no put or next retry. Its install\n2124\t   children are stamped and stepped in `:running` only.\"\n2125\t  [state]\n2126\t  (let [wait-set (:wait-set state)]\n2127\t    (if (and (empty? wait-set) (empty? (:installs state)))\n2128\t      state\n2129\t      (let [state (poll-links state\n2130\t                              (filterv link-entry? wait-set)\n2131\t                              (remove link-entry? wait-set))\n2132\t            wait-set (:wait-set state)\n2133\t            gated? (some? (vm/gate-mode state))\n2134\t            state (if gated?\n2135\t                    state\n2136\t                    (poll-ffi-responses state\n2137\t                                        (filterv ffi-response-entry? wait-set)\n2138\t                                        (remove ffi-response-entry?\n2139\t                                                wait-set)))\n2140\t            wait-set (:wait-set state)\n2141\t            engine-polled? (some-fn link-entry?\n2142\t                                    ffi-response-entry?\n2143\t                                    observe-entry?\n2144\t                                    (fn [e]\n2145\t                                      (and gated?\n2146\t                                           (contains? #{:put :next}\n2147\t                                                      (:reason e)))))\n2148\t            streams (filterv (complement engine-polled?) wait-set)\n2149\t            {:keys [woken store], :as result}\n2150\t            (waitset/check {:waiting streams}\n2151\t                           waitset-resolver\n2152\t                           (:resources state))\n2153\t            v (assoc state\n2154\t                     :resources store\n2155\t                     :wait-set (into (:waiting (:waitset result))\n2156\t                                     (filter engine-polled?)\n2157\t                                     wait-set))]\n2158\t        (update v\n2159\t                :ready-queue (fnil into [])\n2160\t                (make-woken-run-queue-entries v woken))))))"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72b4f199-a30e-42b5-b648-90d6dc2ab934","uuid":"3d5a4139-a8aa-4155-810e-c9b4e2fa0d50","timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:09:17.106Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc","content":"(defn check-wait-set\n  \"Check wait-set entries against their transports.\n\n   The sweep is `dao.stream.waitset/check` — this engine was that library's\n   seed and is now its first consumer. Every entry is resolved to a live\n   handle and an opaque cursor out of the store by `waitset-resolver` and\n   polled with a synchronous `next` or `append!` — resolution happens per\n   poll, so the stored entry itself never carries a handle. There is no\n   transport-local waking to fall back from: this is the only mechanism.\n\n   Entries are polled one at a time in wait-set order, and a woken reader's\n   successor cursor is written back to the store before the next entry is\n   resolved. Waiters sharing a cursor-ref therefore read distinct values —\n   the value at the cursor wakes the first, its successor wakes the next —\n   instead of every waiter reading the value at the shared pre-poll\n   cursor. An entry that stays waiting is retained in its stored,\n   resource-id form.\n\n   Each woken result's `:status` is stamped onto its ready entry, where\n   `terminal-resume-outcome` reads it: an outcome the immediate operation\n   raises as an error fails the same way when the resume pops it — and a\n   waitset diagnostic, an entry the sweep could not poll at all, raises\n   there too, before any continuation is restored.\n\n   The link wait entries `require` adds (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.2) are\n   polled first, by the engine rather than the stream sweep: a\n   `:link-request` retries its envelope, a `:link-response` advances its\n   own kept cursor to the response carrying its id, and an `:install`\n   waits on its install child. The install children are then stepped in\n   this same round (section 7.3), so a child that halts restores its\n   waiters here; nothing about a child runs inside a restore.\n\n   The FFI response readers are routed next, also outside the stream\n   sweep (`poll-ffi-responses`): a response wakes the reader whose call\n   id it names, never whichever reader its cell reached first.\n\n   A gated machine (any `:yin.k/gate`) observes nothing here: no link\n   retry or scan, no FFI response read, no put or next retry. Its install\n   children are stamped and stepped in `:running` only.\"\n  [state]\n  (let [wait-set (:wait-set state)]\n    (if (and (empty? wait-set) (empty? (:installs state)))\n      state\n      (let [state (poll-links state\n                              (filterv link-entry? wait-set)\n                              (remove link-entry? wait-set))\n            wait-set (:wait-set state)\n            gated? (some? (vm/gate-mode state))\n            state (if gated?\n                    state\n                    (poll-ffi-responses state\n                                        (filterv ffi-response-entry? wait-set)\n                                        (remove ffi-response-entry?\n                                                wait-set)))\n            wait-set (:wait-set state)\n            engine-polled? (some-fn link-entry?\n                                    ffi-response-entry?\n                                    observe-entry?\n                                    (fn [e]\n                                      (and gated?\n                                           (contains? #{:put :next}\n                                                      (:reason e)))))\n            streams (filterv (complement engine-polled?) wait-set)\n            {:keys [woken store], :as result}\n            (waitset/check {:waiting streams}\n                           waitset-resolver\n                           (:resources state))\n            v (assoc state\n                     :resources store\n                     :wait-set (into (:waiting (:waitset result))\n                                     (filter engine-polled?)\n                                     wait-set))]\n        (update v\n                :ready-queue (fnil into [])\n                (make-woken-run-queue-entries v woken))))))","numLines":75,"startLine":2086,"totalLines":2789}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01L6VXy3gV2NqMnxvK9DkUM3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
